# State names every variable value, and this state names a running campaign. It is not a
# secret store, but it is not something to commit either.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example

# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is NOT ignored, deliberately. It pins each provider to an exact
# version and checksum, which is the same reason `package-lock.json` and the exact `ruff`
# pin are committed: a gate that moves on its own is not a gate. An unpinned provider
# would have a plan differ between a laptop and CI on a release nobody made.
